<title>BELGIUM: Belgian beet plantings jump in latest week.</title>
<headline>Belgian beet plantings jump in latest week.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian sugar beet plantings totalled 8,445 hectares, or 8.23 percent of the planned total on March 31, the Belgian sugar beet institute (IRBAB) said.</p>
<p>At the last planting survey on March 24, the planted area totalled 1,565 hectares, or 1.53 percent of the planned area.</p>
<p>The planned area for 1997 is 102,586 hectares, down from 103,849 hectares in 1996.</p>
<p>--Brussels Bureau +322 287 6830</p>
